  "question": {
    "text": "A sample of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> (density 1.787 g <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ) is labelled as 86% by weight. What volume (in mL) of this acid has to be used to make 1 L of 0.2 M <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> ?<br />\r[Report your answer upto two decimal places.]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12.75",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> is 86% by weight<br />So weight of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> = 86 g<br />Weight of solution = 100 g<br />So volume of solution <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1.787</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1.787</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>86</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>98</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1.787</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>15.68</mn></math><br />Let V mL of this <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> are used to prepare 1 L of 0.2 M <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> .<br />So mmoles of concentrated <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math> mmoles of dilute <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math><br />So <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>15.68</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.2</mn></math><br />So V = 12.75 mL.",
